<title>UK: SHELL SAYS SELLS S. AFRICA COAL INTERESTS.</title>
<headline>SHELL SAYS SELLS S. AFRICA COAL INTERESTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell International Ltd said on Tuesday that it had signed a letter of intent to sell its coal interests in South Africa to JCI Ltd of South Africa.</p>
<p>A company spokesman declined to disclose financial details of the agreement.</p>
<p>In a statement Shell said its coal business largely comprised a 50 percent stake in the Rietspruit mine and a stake in the Richards Bay coal terminal. Shell said it would continue to market Rietspruit coal.</p>
<p>The company said it would concentrate &quot;on the core elements of its coal business in Australia and Venezuela,&quot; particularly on the expanding use of coal in power generation.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
